{:fh/id  "FH-SUB-008"
 :fh/law "v/sub during render returns the subscription's current value and records a render-owned read; the SELECTED commit publishes those reads as the bundle's dependency set — exactly the queries read, in render order, each an owned dependency."

 ;; Two ordinary subscription sites over one frame's app-db, read through the
 ;; PUBLIC v/sub rather than the shell's internal observe! port.
 :query-a [:sub/a]
 :query-b [:sub/b]
 :db      {:a 10 :b 20}

 ;; v/sub returns each subscription's current value, in read order.
 :values  [10 20]

 ;; A render owns nothing; the SELECTED commit owns the whole dependency set.
 :before  {:lifecycle :new       :dependency-count 0}
 :after   {:lifecycle :connected :dependency-count 2}}
